{"status":"ready","content":"I need to compute the sample variance of the dataset {9, 14, 5, 4, -20, -13, -5, 13}.\r\n\r\n## Step 1: Find the mean\r\n\r\n$$\\bar{x} = \\frac{9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13}{8}$$\r\n\r\n$$\\bar{x} = \\frac{9 + 14 + 5 + 4 - 20 - 13 - 5 + 13}{8} = \\frac{7}{8}$$\r\n\r\n## Step 2: Calculate each squared deviation from the mean\r\n\r\nFor each value $x_i$, I need $(x_i - \\frac{7}{8})^2$:\r\n\r\n- $(9 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (\\frac{65}{8})^2 = \\frac{4225}{64}$\r\n- $(14 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (\\frac{105}{8})^2 = \\frac{11025}{64}$\r\n- $(5 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (\\frac{33}{8})^2 = \\frac{1089}{64}$\r\n- $(4 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (\\frac{25}{8})^2 = \\frac{625}{64}$\r\n- $(-20 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-\\frac{167}{8})^2 = \\frac{27889}{64}$\r\n- $(-13 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-\\frac{111}{8})^2 = \\frac{12321}{64}$\r\n- $(-5 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-\\frac{47}{8})^2 = \\frac{2209}{64}$\r\n- $(13 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (\\frac{97}{8})^2 = \\frac{9409}{64}$\r\n\r\n## Step 3: Sum the squared deviations\r\n\r\n$$\\sum(x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\frac{4225 + 11025 + 1089 + 625 + 27889 + 12321 + 2209 + 9409}{64}$$\r\n\r\n$$= \\frac{68792}{64} = \\frac{8599}{8}$$\r\n\r\n## Step 4: Calculate sample variance\r\n\r\nThe sample variance uses $n-1$ in the denominator:\r\n\r\n$$s^2 = \\frac{\\sum(x_i - \\bar{x})^2}{n-1} = \\frac{\\frac{8599}{8}}{7} = \\frac{8599}{56}$$\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{\\frac{8599}{56}}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-5/livebench-052-math.txt","size":1290,"mtime":1779366649}